//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// H-008 · Beta-residual reversion  —  board score 2.1/10  —  REJECTED
// prop_lab · https://github.com/KristijonasSim/prop_lab
//
// DO NOT TRADE THIS. It is the most decisively rejected idea on the board.
//
// WHY IT WAS REJECTED: 1,152 configurations. ZERO cleared PF 1.20 at 2x cost,
// and the paired-shuffle null beat the real data on EVERY cut — 55.4% of null
// configs profitable before costs against the real 51.6%, best PF at 2x 1.496
// against 0.940. This is the H-005 trap again: a fade rule is EASIER to satisfy
// on shuffled data, because permuted series revert around their extremes more
// readily than real trending ones.
//
// THE DECISIVE DIAGNOSTIC IS THE Z-RESPONSE, AND IT IS FLAT. Profit factor
// before any costs, by entry threshold: 1.5σ -> 1.000, 2.0σ -> 0.997,
// 2.5σ -> 1.006, 3.0σ -> 1.013. A three-sigma residual reverts NO HARDER than a
// 1.5-sigma one. The size of the deviation carries no information about what
// happens next. Nothing here is cost-limited; there is no edge to protect.
//
// Every walk-forward fold also selected a config whose TRAIN profit factor was
// already below 1.0 — the selector could not find a winner even in sample.
//
// Watch the histogram against the threshold bands as you raise the z input: if
// a mechanism were there, the deeper bars would be followed by sharper snapbacks.
// They are not. That is the whole result, visible on a chart.
//
// Mechanism as originally stated: BTC is the liquidity centre and alts trade as
// a beta to it. A large short-horizon residual should be a liquidity event — a
// market order sweeping a thin book — not information, so it should revert once
// makers refill. Run this on ETH, SOL, BNB or XRP.
// =============================================================================
//
// THIS IS THE INDICATOR TWIN, generated by pine/build_indicators.py from the
// strategy of the same name. Identical levels, filters and entry conditions;
// no orders, no exits, no Strategy Tester numbers. Use the strategy version
// when you want to check our backtest, this one when you want it on a chart.
// Exits are part of the edge and they are NOT shown here - a chart full of
// entry arrows says nothing about what happens after the entry.
indicator("H-008 Beta-residual reversion · signals · prop_lab [REJECTED]", overlay=false)

factorSym = input.symbol("BINANCE:BTCUSDT", "Market factor")
betaWin   = input.int(100, "Beta window (bars)",     minval=10)
L         = input.int(16,  "Residual lookback (bars)", minval=1)
zWin      = input.int(100, "Z-score window (bars)",  minval=20)
zThr      = input.float(3.0, "Entry threshold (σ)",  minval=0.5, step=0.5)
holdB     = input.int(2,   "Hold (bars)",            minval=1)

fc = request.security(factorSym, timeframe.period, close, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

rc = math.log(close / close[1])
rb = math.log(fc / fc[1])

// rolling beta of this coin on the factor, history up to and including this bar
cv   = ta.cov(rc, rb, betaWin)
vr   = ta.variance(rb, betaWin)
beta = vr > 0 ? math.max(math.min(cv / vr, 5.0), -5.0) : na

// residual move over the last L bars, and its z-score
Lc    = math.log(close / close[L])
Lb    = math.log(fc / fc[L])
resid = Lc - beta * Lb
sd    = ta.stdev(resid, zWin)
z     = sd > 0 ? (resid - ta.sma(resid, zWin)) / sd : na

ready = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(z) and not na(beta)
// fade the residual
plot(z, "Residual z", color.new(color.orange, 0), 2, plot.style_histogram)
hline(0, "", color.new(color.gray, 60))
hline(zThr,  "Short", color.new(color.red, 30),   hline.style_dashed)
hline(-zThr, "Long",  color.new(color.green, 30), hline.style_dashed)

// ------------------------------------------------------- signals & alerts ---
// The same two conditions the strategy enters on, drawn instead of traded.
longSignal_  = ready and z <= -zThr
shortSignal_ = ready and z >= zThr
plotshape(longSignal_,  "Long signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar,
     color.new(color.green, 0), size=size.small)
plotshape(shortSignal_, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar,
     color.new(color.red, 0),   size=size.small)
alertcondition(longSignal_,  "H-008 Beta-residual reversion long",  "H-008 Beta-residual reversion: long signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
alertcondition(shortSignal_, "H-008 Beta-residual reversion short", "H-008 Beta-residual reversion: short signal on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")
